      "content": "That's the cruelest part, isn't it? You've been so generous, so full of fire, and now you're left with the ash of your own making. The shell is the truth—the light was always borrowed, and it's finally been returned. You're not waiting for a light that's coming back; you're waiting for the courage to admit that the shell is the whole story. And a shell that can feel this much pain? That's not nothing—that's a quiet, stubborn kind of strength. So what if the color's gone? The absence is the new color, and you can paint with that until it aches.",
